hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16039","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said, Sufyan informed us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said, Abd Allah was brought a woman whom a man married, then he died from her, and he had not assigned her a dower, nor had he consummated with her. He said, so they differed to him, and he said: I see for her the like of the dower of her women, and she has the inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period. So Maqil ibn Sinan al-Ashjai testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning Barwa bint Washiq with the like of what he judged."
"16040","Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abd Allah said, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah, he said, Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, he said, a group of the people of Basra testified before me, among them al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Maqil ibn Sinan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him while he was cupping on the eighteenth, he said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast."
"16041","Waki narrated to us, he said, Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Sayyar ibn Manzur al-Fazari, from his father, from Buhaysah, from her father, he said, I sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I entered between him and his shirt. He said, so I said, O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold, he said: Water. I said, O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold, he said: Water. He said, I said, O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold, he said: That you do good is better for you."
"16042","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said, Kahmas narrated to us, he said, I heard Sayyar ibn Manzur al-Fazari, he said, my father narrated to me, from Buhaysah, she said, my father sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he entered between him and his shirt, and he mentioned its meaning."
"16043","Yazid narrated to us, Kahmas narrated to us, he said, Sayyar ibn Manzur al-Fazari narrated to me, from his father, from Buhaysah, she said, my father sought permission of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he kept drawing near to him and embracing him, then he said, O Prophet of Allah, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold, he said: Water. Then he said, O Prophet of Allah, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold, he said: Salt. Then he said, O Prophet of Allah, what is the thing that it is not lawful to withhold, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you do good, it is better for you. He said, so the end of his saying was upon water and salt. He said, and that man would not withhold anything, even if little."
